Key a named construction's factory lookup on the applied head, not the slot type

Dev accepted the last observation from the named-construction work, in these words: "key
constructionInitializer's factory lookup on the applied head (dotted as spelled, bare against
the definition in effect) instead of the slot type, and add one NamedConstructionTest case with
a parent-typed slot, compiled and run." The interception decided whether a named application
was a factory call by loading the SLOT type and checking for a factory; the thing constructed is
the HEAD. The two coincide at every corpus site, which is why nothing had shown it. A probe
showed the gap: `dyn make domains.terrestrial.Terrestrial domains.terrestrial.Location(latitude:…)`
rendered `Location(latitude = 1.5, …)` — Terrestrial is a domain with no factory, so the lookup
said "not a construction" and the arguments reached Scala unmapped, which Location's `_latitude`
factory refuses. Typing a slot by a parent and constructing a child is ordinary authoring.

constructionInitializer now takes only the value and asks loadDracoType about the head leaf —
dotted as spelled, or bare and resolved against the definition in effect, exactly as the slot
type was resolved since 9779e39; a head that is not a name leaf is no construction. The slot
type plays no part in the decision, as it never did on the positional path; initializer and
dynResult pass the value alone. Corpus impact is nil by construction: at the three named sites
(aerial/Input, terrestrial/Output, world/Observable) and in Consumer the head names the
definition the slot named, and all four regenerate byte-identical — Input and Output to the
pre-repair engine's output, Observable and Consumer to their committed Scala.

NamedConstructionTest gains the accepted fifth case: a domains.world probe whose slot is the
parent domain Terrestrial and whose head constructs Location with named arguments, asserted to
map `_latitude`, `_longitude`, `_elevationMetres`, compiled with the runtime compiler, run, and
its result checked to be a Location carrying the authored values. This closes the three
observations raised on October 26; none remains preserved from the named-construction thread.

